# Architecture Rules

## Architecture

The project follows the approved architecture:

Presentation
    ↓
Application
    ↓
Domain

Infrastructure provides implementations for required external concerns.

Domain must not depend on Presentation.

Domain must not depend directly on infrastructure details.

## Domain

Domain contains:

- game rules;
- state;
- entities;
- value objects;
- domain calculations;
- domain decisions.

Domain must not contain:

- rendering;
- keyboard handling;
- file system access;
- UI widgets;
- engine-specific presentation logic.

## Application

Application coordinates use cases and system interactions.

Application may depend on domain.

Application must not contain rendering logic.

## Presentation

Presentation handles:

- input;
- rendering;
- UI;
- presentation state.

Presentation must not become the source of truth for game rules.

## Infrastructure

Infrastructure handles technical details such as:

- persistence;
- file access;
- external resources;
- engine-specific infrastructure concerns.

## Rule

Do not create an abstraction merely because it is theoretically useful.

Create abstractions when they protect a real architectural boundary.